en.summary:
Promote community health by helping individuals adopt healthy behaviors; serve as an advocate for individuals' health needs by helping community residents communicate effectively with medical providers or social service agencies; serve as a liaison or advocate and implement programs that promote, maintain, and improve individual and overall community health; may provide health-related preventive services such as blood pressure, glaucoma, and hearing screening; may collect data to help identify community health needs: advise clients
or community groups on self-care and general health and risk prevention and hygiene and screening; identify the specific health care needs of individuals in a community or target area and refer community members to the services they need; develop plans or formal contracts with individuals and families and community groups to improve overall health; advocate to government agencies or health service providers about individual or community health needs and feed back service accessibility; conduct basic screening and carry out basic preventive procedures such as immunization and first aid; make home visits to pregnant women and newborns or other high-risk individuals and monitor the nutrition of high-risk groups; 
maintain client files and contact clients to confirm that actions are completed; participate in community meetings and health fairs and distribute educational materials; and report suspected child or elder abuse and neglect and threat of harm to the competent authority as needed.
